*Spin-Orbit Splitting:* The spin-orbit interaction energy is given by $E_("SO") = lambda/2 [J(J+1) - L(L+1) - S(S+1)]$, where $lambda$ is the coupling constant. The Landé interval rule relates the energy difference between adjacent fine-structure levels to the coupling constant.
